@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: why the sbx egress row shows sbx's baselines, read-only, instead of proveo's tiers
' covers: internal/sbx/sbx.go
' covers: internal/run/choices.go
' covers: internal/sbx/baseline_test.go
'
' ── THE ROW WAS DEAD ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' On the sbx backend the egress axis offered open | allowlist | review and none
' of the three did anything. sandbox.Spec derives the Kit allowlist from the
' harness capabilities and the detected providers and NEVER consults the tier, so
' open and allowlist produce an identical sandbox; review is not supported there
' at all and falls back to docker. A three-option risk axis on which nothing
' moves is worse than no axis: it tells the operator they chose a posture.
'
' ── WHAT ACTUALLY GOVERNS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
' sbx's GLOBAL network baseline — allow-all | balanced | deny-all. It is the only
' lever, and that is a property of how sbx composes policy, not a proveo choice:
'   * a Kit ADDS allow rules on top of the baseline; it cannot subtract.
'   * a per-sandbox deny cannot express "only the allowlist", because deny beats
'     allow — `sbx policy deny network --sandbox X "**"` blocks the allowlist too.
' So on an allow-all host the Kit allowlist ADDS REACH rather than limiting it,
' and proveo's own warning has said exactly that on every run for some time. The
' row now says it in the place the operator is actually looking.
'
' ── DISPLAY ONLY, AND THAT IS THE POINT ────────────────────────────────────
' The row is LOCKED. proveo reports the baseline and never sets it:
'   * it is host-wide, shared by every sandbox including ones proveo never
'     started, so a per-run prompt would rewrite other people's runs;
'   * changing it needs `sbx policy reset`, which clears EVERY policy on the host;
'   * and offering it as a per-run choice would teach the wrong intuition — that
'     this is a property of the container in front of you. It is not.
' The change hint is one sample, identical for every baseline. It carries the
' reset because `sbx policy init` alone is REJECTED once a host is initialized —
' measured: "global network policy is already initialized; use sbx policy reset
' first to change it". A hint without the reset would print a command that fails.
'
' ── READING IT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' From sbx, not by probing. `sbx policy check` can only separate allow-all from
' "something stricter", because balanced and deny-all both deny an unallowlisted
' host. `sbx policy inspect local-policy` prints the rules, and the network rows
' classify structurally:
'   allow **          -> allow-all
'   no network allow  -> deny-all
'   specific allows   -> balanced
' Unreadable stays UNREADABLE. Naming a baseline proveo could not read would put a
' boundary in front of the operator that may not exist — the same failure the dead
' row committed, in the other direction.
'
' MEASURED HOW FAR: only allow-all was observable on the development host, because
' changing the baseline needs the destructive reset. The other two fixtures are
' built from the same table shape; internal/sbx TestPolicyBaselineLive (tag
' livesbx) is what catches sbx changing that table.
'
' STILL OPEN: posture.EnforcedBy says "sbx — Kit network allowlist + credential
' proxy" whatever the baseline is, which overstates on an allow-all host. Left
' unchanged deliberately: the same measurement governs whether an sbx sandbox's
' own docker daemon can leave the Kit allowlist, which is unsettled.
title The sbx egress row — showing what governs, not what proveo intends

participant "operator" as OP <<app>>
participant "proveo\negressRow" as ROW <<app>>
participant "sbx policy\ninspect local-policy" as SBX <<cloud>>
participant "the Kit\nallowlist" as KIT <<data>>

OP ARROW_MAIN ROW : run <harness> (sbx backend)
ROW ARROW_MAIN SBX : read the global baseline
SBX ARROW_MAIN ROW : allow ** -> allow-all
ROW ARROW_ERROR OP : locked row, current value shown,\none runnable command to change it
KIT ARROW_OPTIONAL SBX : adds allow rules ON TOP\n(cannot subtract)

note over ROW
  **Docker is untouched.** The tier stays real and
  selectable there, enforced by the Squid and MITM
  sidecars. ""--egress-mode"" keeps its canonical
  values on both backends, so nothing the
  in-container gate parses changed (D4).
end note

note over SBX
  **Deny beats allow.** That one rule is why the
  baseline is the only lever: no per-sandbox rule
  means "confine to the allowlist", because a deny
  broad enough to confine also blocks the
  allowlist it was meant to leave open.
end note
@enduml
